.TH BACKDROP 1 "2026-11-13" "backdrop 2.81.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
backdrop \- Wallpaper and screensaver manager: curate images and videos from free sources and display them with mpv
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbackdrop\fR [\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
\fBbackdrop\fR \fB\-\-help\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
backdrop collects images and videos from API\-based sources (Pexels first) and local folders into a library, and shows them as the X11 desktop wallpaper through one mpv per monitor, each wrapped by xwinwrap and driven over mpv's JSON IPC socket. A daemon owns those processes: it follows monitor hotplug, restarts mpv when it exits or stops answering, reshuffles the playlist, limits video play time, and with the visualizer section runs GLava, sleeve or projectM visualizers above the wallpaper.
.PP
Items are rated as they play: keep (1 to 3) moves an item into the library, skip moves it to the trash, and undo puts the last rating back. Status lives in the database, not in folders. The rofi menu (backdrop menu) and the web interface (backdrop web) drive the same actions.
.PP
With no command, backdrop prints the status. Most commands act on the monitor under the pointer; \-\-monitor picks another. Commands that print an item or a list take \-\-json for scripts (docs/specs/json.md).
.SH COMMANDS
